Let word be "()[]{}".
Let n be the number of characters in word.
Let stack be an empty list of whole numbers.
Let valid be true.

For every i from 0 to n - 1:
    Let c be character i of word.
    If c is 40 or c is 91 or c is 123:
        Append c to stack.
    Otherwise:
        Let size be count of stack.
        If size is 0:
            Set valid to false.
        Otherwise:
            Let top be item (size - 1) of stack.
            Remove the last item from stack.
            If c is 41 and top is not 40, set valid to false.
            If c is 93 and top is not 91, set valid to false.
            If c is 125 and top is not 123, set valid to false.

Let final size be count of stack.
If final size is not 0:
    Set valid to false.
Print valid.
